{
  "name": "AI Jira Ticket Autopilot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🎯 AI JIRA TICKET AUTOPILOT\n**What it does:** Every hour → fetches open Jira tickets → dedupes against Google Sheets → an AI agent triages each ticket with structured output → safe tickets get auto-resolved (Jira comment + Done transition + `ai-resolved` label) → risky tickets get escalated to a human → your team gets one Telegram digest.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- Jira Cloud (free at atlassian.com) + an API token (Atlassian account → Security → API tokens)\n- OpenAI API key (platform.openai.com)\n- Google Sheets OAuth2 credential\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID (@BotFather → /newbot)\n\n**Status flow in Sheets:** `NEW` → `TRIAGED` → `RESOLVED` / `ESCALATED`",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 5980,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "eb555ddb-a308-41c5-a457-884d40bf8e5c",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Fetch open Jira tickets\nHourly schedule trigger → Basic-auth header built from your Jira email + API token → Jira REST API `/rest/api/3/search` with JQL `project=<key> AND status in (\"To Do\",\"Open\")` → normalize key/summary/description/priority/reporter/URL.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1160,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "8f8e84a8-e7fb-4ec4-81b9-dd709b9c2e27",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — Dedupe + log to Google Sheets\nRead already-logged ticket keys → keep only new tickets → append rows with status `NEW`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1140,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "ebcd6724-88a7-4941-80e1-461e6bbdc2d8",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — AI triage with structured output\nAI Ticket Triage Agent (gpt-4o-mini) decides per ticket: auto-resolve or escalate — returns can_resolve, confidence 0–100, category, resolution comment, escalation reason via a Structured Output Parser → sheet flips to `TRIAGED`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 980,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "d9c2d13d-731e-48a0-85bc-8b77f5db961b",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2120,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Auto-resolve / escalate gate\n`IF — Auto-Resolve?` passes only can_resolve=true AND confidence ≥ your threshold.\nTRUE: post the AI's resolution comment → look up the Jira \"Done\" transition → transition the ticket → add your `ai-resolved` label → sheet flips to `RESOLVED`.\nFALSE: sheet flips to `ESCALATED` with the AI's escalation reason for a human.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 1640,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "7fe34ff4-ccf6-4114-b63b-7615655718c5",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3040,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 5 — Team digest + Telegram\nBoth branches merge → one digest built (resolved count + escalated count + per-ticket lines with links) → Telegram to your team.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1020,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b986cd09-29b5-4359-855e-c2c6de32b85c",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4720,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 1
            }
